---
title: Tamago Sando
servings: 2
cuisine: Japanese
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mba10nKOdr8
image: https://cdn.justonecookbook.com/spai/q_glossy+ret_img+to_auto/www.justonecookbook.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/03/Tamago-Sando-II.jpg
---

Split @hard boiled eggs{2} in half, putting the yolk in a #small bowl{} and the whites aside for later on a paper towel.

Using a spoon, mash the yolk to break it down a bit.

Add @kewpie mayo{2%tbsp}, @salt{}(to taste), and @pepper{}(to taste). Mix until combined.

Carefully chop the egg whites into fine pieces, avoiding cutting the paper towel.

> We use a paper towel to absorb the moisture from the egg whites as we cut them.

Add the egg whites back to the yolk mixture and mix until combined. 

Combine @butter{10%g}(melted) with @yellow mustard{1/2%tsp}.

Spread butter mixture on oen side of each slice of @bread{4}. Then spread the egg mixture on top.

> A similar recipe from our favorite JustOneCookbook can be found here: https://www.justonecookbook.com/japanese-egg-sandwich-tamago-sando/